llmsInstallationContent:
ZeroMind is a remote MCP server that drives a 3D engine running in the user's browser. Link the machine once with `zeromind link`, then install via Cline's MCP Servers UI (Command Palette → "Cline: MCP Servers" → "Configure MCP Servers"):
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "zeromind": {
      "type": "streamableHttp",
      "url": "https://origozero.ai/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer <this machine's install_secret>",
        "X-ZM-Harness": "cline"
      },
      "disabled": false,
      "autoApprove": []
    }
  }
}
```
The install secret is the `install_secret` in `~/.config/zero/session.json` (`%APPDATA%/zero/session.json` on Windows); `zeromind install cline` writes the whole entry for you.
Then drop the agent rule:
```
npx @origozero/zeromind install cline
```
Or write `.clinerules/zeromind.md` yourself with the content of https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OrigoZero/zeromind-plugin/main/templates/manual.md

Run `zeromind link` first if this machine has never been linked — it opens a one-time device-code approval at https://origozero.ai/link.
